<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The camera half of the app, merged in only for the SCANNER flavour.

  Delivery scans bag QR codes and Store scans garments and bags; the Customer
  app never scans, and an app that asks for a camera it never opens is one
  people are right to distrust. So the permission is not "declared and unused"
  in the customer build — it is absent from it.

  A manifest placeholder cannot do this: the merger reads tools:node before
  placeholders are substituted, so `tools:node="${...}"` fails the build. A
  flavour overlay is the mechanism that actually exists for it.

  Declaring the permission still does not grant it. MainActivity asks Android
  at the moment of the first scan and forwards ONLY that grant to the web
  layer, denying every other resource the page asks for.

  required="false" so the build still installs on a device with no camera.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera" android:required="false" />
</manifest>
